# Response headers for the static assets, read by Workers at the edge. Vite
# copies this file into dist/ and Workers parses it there; it is never served.
#
# The devlog's thirty-seven media files are transcoded by hand, committed, and
# named from the slug table in tools/devlog/embeds.ts. They do not change: a
# rebuild produces the same bytes from the same export. Served on the Workers
# default of `max-age=0, must-revalidate` they still cost every returning
# reader forty conditional round trips before the article can finish drawing.
#
# The price of `immutable` is that these names are not content-hashed, so a
# file that IS re-encoded keeps its old bytes in caches for up to a year. That
# makes it a rule rather than a caveat: changing one of these files means
# changing its slug in embeds.ts, which changes its URL. The slug table is
# where that is enforced, and it is the same table the build already fails on.
/writing/rise-and-shine/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
